late)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member types","id":"Member_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Helper types","id":"Helper_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"types","title":"Type support (basic types, RTTI)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::add_cv, std::add_const, std::add_volatile","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"3 declarations; revisions: since C++11. Provides the member typedef type which is the same as T, except it has a cv-qualifier added (unless T is a function, a…"},{"label":"Member types","children":[{"label":"type","note":"the type T with the cv-qualifier"}]},{"label":"Helper types"},{"label":"Possible implementation"},{"label":"Notes","note":"These transformation traits can be used to establish non-deduced contexts in template argument deduction:"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"is_const","note":"checks if a type is const-qualified"},{"label":"is_volatile","note":"checks if a type is volatile-qualified"},{"label":"remove_cv, remove_const, remove_volatile","note":"removes const and/or volatile specifiers from the given type"},{"label":"as_const","note":"obtains a reference to const to its argument"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++14","C++17"],"wordCount":303,"codeBlockCount":4}
